cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite the software release and the accompanying
  manuscript listed in README.md. Use the Zenodo DOI for the exact released
  version used in your analysis.
title: "Armed conflict and reported disease outbreaks: a global country-year analysis — replication code"
abstract: >-
  Replication code for a global country-year analysis of armed conflict and the
  composition of WHO-reported infectious disease outbreaks, 1996–2024. It links
  WHO Disease Outbreak News records to the UCDP/PRIO Armed Conflict Dataset v25.1
  and World Development Indicators. The panel covers 236 countries and territories
  and contains 6,756 country-years after country-existence exclusions; 5,617 have
  complete controls. Disease-specific estimation samples vary. The code estimates
  fixed-effects models of reported disease-category presence and counts, with
  lagged exposures, sensitivity analyses, FDR adjustment and country bootstrap
  intervals. The outcomes describe reporting, not population outbreak incidence.
